MID_LGV_3_M03_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kai_m01_001: I'm grown now, and I'm stronger, so I can do more\nfor you.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kai_m01_002: Please rely on me for anything, Promised One! I'll do\neverything in my power to accomplish it.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kai_m01_003: I want to pay you back for all you've done for us.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Kai_m01: <BLN>Rely on me for anything!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Bel_m01_001: I resided in Dagsion for quite a while... In the inside\nof its dungeon, granted.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Bel_m01_002: Still, I had an affinity for the capital and the people\nwho lived here.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Bel_m01_003: I wish I'd had more time with them while they lived.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Bel_m01: <BLN>I spent years in the dungeon.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dit_m01_001: You tremble...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dit_m01_002: Not you, Promised One. Answerer. It longs for battle.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dit_m01_003: But there is more. It thirsts to settle things with you.\nI can tell...
MID_LGA_3_M03_Dit_m01: <BLN>I can tell...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tal_m01_001: Ugh... I can't stand the sight of blood. In fact, I'd\nprefer to leave aaaall the dirty work to others.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tal_m01_002: But those who fight for me keep dying, you see.\nSo I've decided to end this myself.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tal_m01_003: Because I'm sick of all this death. If they want my\nway of life, they're gonna have to take it.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Tal_m01: <BLN>I hate blood...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Orh_m01_001: I really wanted to help soldiers train.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Orh_m01_002: As so, as my body is extremely durable, I said that\nthey could practice by striking me.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Orh_m01_003: No one wanted to do it. I think it's a worthwhile\nidea though!
MID_LGA_3_M03_Orh_m01: <BLN>I wouldn't mind at all!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Seo_m01_001: As part of our defense of Saramis, I am having the\nDanann Sea patrolled.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Seo_m01_002: Ships crewed by the risen dead have been appearing\noften in Dagdan waters to attack the living.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Seo_m01_003: Let me know if you anticipate a battle at sea. You\nwill see the Saraminian navy at their best.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Seo_m01: <BLN>We are patrolling the sea.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Led_m01_001: I can control Obsidian much better now than I ever\ncould before.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Led_m01_002: I don't know if that means my skills have improved,\nor that my soul is becoming intertwined with it...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Led_m01_003: Heh. I guess it doesn't matter—as long as you're here\nto stop me if I lose my faculties.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Led_m01: <BLN>Truth be told...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Anh_m01_001: In the time since we liberated the capital, I've been\ncontinuously surprised by the resilience of humans.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Anh_m01_002: Even with their world in ruins, they still keep\nfighting to live another day.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Anh_m01_003: They're teaching me so much about resilience. I'll do\neverything I can to protect them in return.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Anh_m01: <BLN>They still keep fighting.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tia_m01_001: Humans, gods, risen dead, demon gods. The enemies\nonly seem to get stronger as we fight...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tia_m01_002: But it's a strategist's job to handle all these problems!\nI won't let them wear me down!
MID_LGA_3_M03_Tia_m01: <BLN>It's my job!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Pet_m01_001: When I was younger, I was never really motivated to\ndo much of anything.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Pet_m01_002: I mean, I only left home to follow my friends.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Pet_m01_003: Now, here I am, fighting to save the world. I guess\nyou never know what life will bring, huh?
MID_LGA_3_M03_Pet_m01: <BLN>I was never really motivated...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hur_m01_001: They're distributing food to folks in Dagsion who\ndon't have homes or anything to eat.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hur_m01_002: I help out sometimes. Chatting while cooking makes\nfor a nice break from the rest of reality.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Hur_m01: <BLN>Makes for a nice break...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Max_m01_001: I'm young for a knight, and not very skilled. Plenty of\nthe knights in Brezarant's history are better.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Max_m01_002: But...most of them are dead.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Max_m01_003: I don't know how I ended up here, but I'll do what I\ncan to live up to their memory.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Max_m01: <BLN>I can't bring them shame.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Gol_m01_001: I still can't believe Gabriel's gone.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Gol_m01_002: What I'd do to see him again, even as one of the\nrisen dead. But then... No! I'd have to kill him!
MID_LGA_3_M03_Gol_m01: <BLN>It makes no sense!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Gat_m01_001: It was surprising enough when I first saw the dead\nbecome Balor's minions.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Gat_m01_002: But the horses as well? And the orniuses?
MID_LGV_3_M03_Gat_m01_003: I suppose the bond between rider and steed is truly\nunbreakable, even in death...
MID_LGA_3_M03_Gat_m01: <BLN>I was shocked.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dan_m01_001: Imagine the sheer variety of experiences being had\nby the fighters here.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dan_m01_002: The war with Balor is facing each of them with their\nown fears, losses, and impossible decisions...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dan_m01_003: From the generals to the lowliest soldiers. And you\nas well, Promised One! Bear it in mind, would you?
MID_LGA_3_M03_Dan_m01: <BLN>All the different perspectives!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fab_m01_001: As I sketched the local flora, a boy I had never seen\nbefore emerged from the brush and offered me seeds.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fab_m01_002: How ridiculous! We are at war. Anything that grows\nis likely to be trampled by soldiers before long.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fab_m01_003: I will sow these seeds once the war is over though.\nI admit that I am curious what may grow.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Fab_m01: <BLN>As I sketched, a boy...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Esm_m01_001: I was fighting to protect one of the villages and they\noffered me food. "You must be hungry. Take it."
MID_LGV_3_M03_Esm_m01_002: I tried to tell them I didn't need it, but they wouldn't\nlisten to me.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Esm_m01_003: Thing is, they were the ones who were hungry. They\njust wanted to thank me.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Esm_m01_004: So I got to work fishing so we could all eat. What\nelse could I do?
MID_LGA_3_M03_Esm_m01: <BLN>What else could I do?
MID_LGV_3_M03_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Urs_m01_001: A few children nearby asked me to read to them.\nWith the scarcity of bards, I suppose it makes sense.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Urs_m01_002: Growing up, I considered reading a solitary activity.\nThis was different, I enjoyed it.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Urs_m01_003: After the war is over, perhaps reading to younglings\ncan become a new hobby.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Urs_m01: <BLN>It was very refreshing.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sim_m01_001: The dead we've been fighting... I knew some of these\nguys in life. Not well, but it still bothers me.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sim_m01_002: I know it shouldn't. I mean, they're already dead so\nwhat's it matter if they get killed again?
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sim_m01_003: We can't go easy on them, you hear? Even if they're\ndead, they deserve to be put down with honor.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Sim_m01: <BLN>It has to be done.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lou_m01_001: Fighting the risen dead is so exhausting! Still, there's\none silver lining to it.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lou_m01_002: The corpses disappear! They reek while they're here,\nbut once they're gone, so is the smell.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lou_m01_003: It's way nicer than fighting regular enemies that just\nlie around after the battle.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Lou_m01: <BLN>Fighting the risen dead...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fia_m01_001: I had a feeling while eating with Centurio once...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fia_m01_002: His attitude still hadn't changed from when we\nfirst met.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fia_m01_003: And I thought...maybe he's worried that I won't be\nable to take care of myself.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Fia_m01: <BLN>Centurio...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Die_m01_001: I don't want to be known as part of a "Promised\nArmy" or anything. I'm a Har Hali warrior, that's all.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Die_m01_002: So, I won't work for you, but I'll be glad to lend a\nhand. Just be sure to utilize me well.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Die_m01: <BLN>I'll lend a hand.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lor_m01_001: I was pretty scared at first, seeing the dead come\nback to life and attack us.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lor_m01_002: But after battling them so much, I'm not nearly as\nfreaked out as I was.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lor_m01_003: Not that I think any of this is something we should\nget used to!
MID_LGA_3_M03_Lor_m01: <BLN>I used to be scared...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Set_m01_001: It seems that the temples have lost much of their\nrelevance, though many gods are still alive.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Set_m01_002: Though I'm a traveler in this strange land, I'm glad\nto see them around. They're needed now.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Set_m01: <BLN>I'm glad to see...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nin_m01_001: I have observed that Credna has been working\nwithout tire these past few years.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nin_m01_002: He's distributed weapons, though mainly around\nBrezarant where his main temple is located.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nin_m01_003: He seems quite busy right now, but I always enjoy\nhearing stories at his side.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Nin_m01: <BLN>Credna's been quite busy.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Bon_m01_001: How quickly we went from honored guests here\nto invaders.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Bon_m01_002: Seeing the damage here reminds me of the War of\nGrania, when we won entry into Fort Zanbar.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Bon_m01_003: The imperials were our enemies, but I feel sorrow\nfor them. For we have now both suffered massacres.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Bon_m01: <BLN>The people of Dagsion...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tob_m01_001: Even with things this bad—maybe BECAUSE things\nare this bad—you gotta appreciate a good drink!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tob_m01_002: Booze has always been a warrior's friend. However\nbad a battle gets, we've got that to look forward to!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tob_m01_003: So three cheers for grapes, honey, and water!\nNature's gifts that keep us goin'!
MID_LGA_3_M03_Tob_m01: <BLN>It's somethin' to live for!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lil_m01_001: Even now, I haven't forgotten about saving up my\nmoney. I still dream of buying back the family home.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lil_m01_002: But none of that's gonna happen until we bring peace\nback not just to Saramis, but the whole world.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lil_m01_003: So I'm willing to fight a little cheaper than I used to.\nNever for free, though. You can bank on that.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Lil_m01: <BLN>Peace first, money later.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lys_m01_001: Even in this fallen world, chatting with the ladies\ntends to pick up my spirits.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Lys_m01_002: Would you care to join in, Promised One? Don't\nworry—I never let it get too serious.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Lys_m01: <BLN>Even in this fallen world...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Buc_m01_001: Our army's composed of soldiers, mercenaries, and\nvolunteers from across the region.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Buc_m01_002: Which means not everyone has much experience.\nThe volunteers, especially, need constant training...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Buc_m01_003: But I'll do my best to instruct them as well as I can,\nso that they don't go and get killed.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Buc_m01: <BLN>Leave it to me.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sci_m01_001: It is when they are most conscious of their mortality\nthat humans are most given to ardor.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sci_m01_002: I've learned this firsthand from night after night with\nthe ladies. They're positively clinging to me!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sci_m01_003: One hopes they can at least set aside their fear of\ndeath during our time together.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Sci_m01: <BLN>Fear can lead to passion.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Moo_m01_001: I know the Order of Mithras used their knowledge of\nalchemy to do this to the world.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Moo_m01_002: But...I don't think it's inherently bad to study a\nsubject and learn things.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Moo_m01_003: I mean, I've always loved cooking, and that's brought\nme to a lot of discoveries about medicinal herbs.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Moo_m01_004: And it helps people! So, I'll keep trying to be a model\nfor how learning can be a force for good.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Moo_m01: <BLN>The Order of Mithras.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mic_m01_001: This army of yours is full of rejects and\ngood-for-nothings. It keeps me on my toes. I like it!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mic_m01_002: I've got my hands full straightening 'em all out.\nSchool of hard knocks, instructor Mikaela Redblade!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mic_m01_003: That said, they're adorable. And they have plenty\nof fighting spirit.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Mic_m01: <BLN>It's never boring.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Oly_m01_001: In the past, if I tore my clothes, I'd buy new ones,\nor ask an artisan to mend them.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Oly_m01_002: With this shortage of materials—and people!—that's\nan impossibility. And sadly, I'm lousy at sewing...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Oly_m01_003: I am a maven with the strings of an instrument!\nWhy can I not convince thread to obey my fingers?
MID_LGA_3_M03_Oly_m01: <BLN>Why?!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Naz_m01_001: Seeing the imperial capital busted up reminds me of\nback in the village.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Naz_m01_002: Guess I'll teach the people of this city how to live in\ntimes like these. I don't think I got any other choice.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Naz_m01_003: People gotta learn how to be careful hunting. Or how\nthey can eat insects if they can't get other food.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Naz_m01: <BLN>Guess I'll teach them how to live.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sar_m01_001: The number of orphans has grown so in these\npast several years of chaos.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sar_m01_002: I'm always happy to look after children. Please don't\nhesitate to ask.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sar_m01_003: I'll do what I can to make all of the children happy,\nespecially the ones who are hurting.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Sar_m01: <BLN>I will look after children...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dai_m01_001: The world's a mess. There's hardly even any\nrestaurants anymore. Less food all around.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dai_m01_002: But what we got tastes better than when we were\nfighting Dagda. I wonder why?
MID_LGV_3_M03_Dai_m01_003: I guess it's because eating with others makes food\nbetter, even when life is the worst otherwise.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Dai_m01: <BLN>I wonder why?
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hal_m01_001: Back before the Heroic Games, I performed all over\nDagda as a member of a circus troupe.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hal_m01_002: We visited villages all over the place. I can remember\nthe faces of some of our audience members...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hal_m01_003: I hope they're all OK. I want the world to be peaceful\nagain just as soon as it can.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Hal_m01: <BLN>I want peace soon.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Guj_m01_001: Hey, so, this is a difficult thing to just come out\nand say.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Guj_m01_002: But...I'm dead. I have been for a while.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Guj_m01_003: Hey, can't you show some kind of reaction? Wow,\nit's really hard to get a rise out of you.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Guj_m01: <BLN>This is difficult to admit...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Yan_m01_001: Nobody can dig a well with a parched throat, nor\ntill a field on an empty stomach.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Yan_m01_002: Similarly, nobody should fight without training, nor\nbattle without tactical planning.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Yan_m01_003: Personally, I shouldn't do any of these things without\nmy favorite tipple! I have stocked up, rest assured.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Yan_m01: <BLN>I am well prepared!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Iio_m01_001: Father was a man of few words. He used to show\nme how to act with actions.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Iio_m01_002: He'd get his orders, don his armor, and without a\nword ride Rocinan toward battle in haste.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Iio_m01_003: I suppose he's similar to you in some ways. I'd have\nliked for you to meet him when he was alive.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Iio_m01: <BLN>My father...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Pep_m01_001: Though nature spirits can show mercy or brutality,\nBrigid's people live in commune with them.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Pep_m01_002: Balor, however, is a demon god who brings nothing\nbut calamity. We know his time will come to an end!
MID_LGA_3_M03_Pep_m01: <BLN>We know it absolutely!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Noc_m01_001: I feel like I'm in fighting form all the time now...\nbecause I'm in lots of good fights.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Noc_m01_002: Doing what I do well makes me happy, which helps\nme deal with so much sadness I see in the city.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Noc_m01: <BLN>Fighting is fun!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sop_m01_001: When I look at the statue of Solel, it reminds me\nof all kinds of things about the temple.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sop_m01_002: I hope all the priests are doing OK. I wonder if Anna\nthinks about what we've lost too?
MID_LGV_3_M03_Sop_m01_003: It'd probably make her unhappy to think about it any\nmore than she is. I'll ask her after we end the war.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Sop_m01: <BLN>The statue makes me think...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cat_m01_001: If my parents or my former lord came back as the\nrisen dead, I'd defeat them without hesitation.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cat_m01_002: I've long known that, on the battlefield, such ties\nvanish when you're on opposing sides.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cat_m01_003: In fact, my lord taught me that, and those words\nlive on in my heart.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Cat_m01: <BLN>I know this for certain.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ned_m01_001: Even after the underworld appeared in our world,\nI tried to get fair compensation as I fought.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ned_m01_002: I'd defend a village in exchange for a place to\nsleep or a simple meal—that's all.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ned_m01_003: It's enough for me, frankly, if both sides of that\ntransaction get what they need to keep living.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Ned_m01: <BLN>Fair compensation...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Zac_m01_001: This lady who was getting attacked by the risen\ndead asked me to help. Me! A bandit!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Zac_m01_002: It really must be the end of the world. That...and\nwhen I stole her purse, there was nothing in it!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Zac_m01_003: I'm sick of feeling so crummy all the time. The end\nof this war can't come soon enough...
MID_LGA_3_M03_Zac_m01: <BLN>It's the end of the world!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Maj_m01_001: It's just unfair, all these folks turnin' into dragons!\nDagda did that too!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Maj_m01_002: What'd they eat to get like that—huge hunks of\nmeat or somethin'?
MID_LGA_3_M03_Maj_m01: <BLN>It's unfair!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ven_m01_001: How long's this war going to go on for? I've got one\nfoot in the grave as it is!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ven_m01_002: It'd be tragic if I died and joined the risen dead. The\ngreat General Benditz deserves better!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ven_m01_003: And I'd be even more terrifying than Balor. So, let's\nget these recruits in gear. They've got to end this!
MID_LGA_3_M03_Ven_m01: <BLN>These recruits!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ini_m01_001: When I see one of the risen dead, I look a little\ncloser to see if it's someone I know.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ini_m01_002: But then I end up thinking I couldn't want to fight\nsomeone like that in battle.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ini_m01_003: I've got no business calling myself a professional\nmercenary... I've got to pull it together.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Ini_m01: <BLN>I've got to pull it together...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Jas_m01_001: I see familiar faces among the risen dead.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Jas_m01_002: Sometimes it's someone I haven't seen in a long\ntime, and now they're dead. That's...unnerving.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Jas_m01_003: What unhappy reunions. I hope I don't have any\nmore of those.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Jas_m01: <BLN>I see them sometimes.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ale_m01_001: They say that the Order of Mithras was behind all\nof this happening.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ale_m01_002: Many people were lured in to the Order with\npromises and couldn't leave. They're victims too.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ale_m01_003: I wish I could have helped them in some way before\nthey ever fell into such evil influence.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Ale_m01: <BLN>I could have done something.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cen_m01_001: Ordinarily, temple forces should have worked\ntogether to handle the risen dead.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cen_m01_002: But, after splitting our forces in the previous battle,\nwe aren't yet acting in a coordinated manner.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cen_m01_003: Thank you, Promised One, for your help in fixing the\nsituation. You're worthy of all the praise you receive.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Cen_m01: <BLN>Thank you, Promised One...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kir_m01_001: What's the difference between the risen dead and\na ghost? Why can I defeat one, not the other?!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kir_m01_002: Tell me, Balor! I beg you, divine one! Why can't I\ndefeat the ghosts that torment me?!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kir_m01_003: Hmm... Well... I should have guessed that I'm not\ngoing to get an answer.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Kir_m01: <BLN>Tell me, please!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nuz_m01_001: You are strong indeed, Promised One, if you are\ncapable of breaking the underworld gates.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nuz_m01_002: The Har Hali revere strength. Our allegiance to the\ndemon god Balor has changed, but that has not.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nuz_m01_003: My people will faithfully carry out any command\nyou give them.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Nuz_m01: <BLN>You are strong indeed.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01_001: A group of children were watching me fearfully\nfrom a distance.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01_002: I told them that if they had something to say to me,\nthen they should speak plainly.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01_003: For some reason, that caused most of them to scatter\nlike rats in the light.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01_004: But one girl remained. She held out a trembling hand\nto offer me a pastry.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01_005: <NCA>"Then what happened?"
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01_006: Well, I was hungry, so I took and ate it.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01_007: The girl seemed rather pleased by this.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01_008: 'Twas a rather meager gift for the Goddess of Fate,\nbut I suppose an offering is an offering.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m01_009: I must be sure to live up to the faith they place\nin me.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Fot_m01: <BLN>What a curious incident.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02_001: It has been weighing on me that we don't know the\npurpose of the key we picked up recently.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02_002: I believe 'twill be important to our victory in some\nway, but I don't yet see how.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02_003: I wish I understood why it nags at me so...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02_004: <NCA>"Could it be related to the progenitor god?"
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02_005: What was that? The progenitor god?
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02_006: Yes, you've hit upon it exactly! 'Twas the temple of\nthe Diadem that eluded me.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02_007: It has been under tight seal by the decree of the\nprogenitor god.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02_008: But if we have the key to remove that seal, what lies\nwithin may be of great assistance to us.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Fot_m02_009: I'll take it upon myself to look into it as soon as I can.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Fot_m02: <BLN>It continues to elude me...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kou_m01_001: I have a Heart Core too, but I didn't get it the way\none is supposed to.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kou_m01_002: I can't use it as effectively as a Mediator can, but I\ncan channel a lot of magical power through it.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Kou_m01_003: Magistra Raksha must have known and recruited me\nspecifically to take advantage of that fact...
MID_LGA_3_M03_Kou_m01: <BLN>I have my own Heart Core.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tro_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tro_m01_001: Humanity's survival is at stake in this war.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tro_m01_002: So it may be inevitable that we're asked to make\nsacrifices in order to win.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Tro_m01_003: But I'm sure all of those gathered here have prepared\nthemselves for that.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Tro_m01: <BLN>This is a war for our survival.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nat_m01_001: My house is back in Arago, and I suppose you'd call\nit prestigious.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nat_m01_002: Still...I was always uncertain about what exactly I\nwas fighting for.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Nat_m01_003: Loyalty, I told myself. It was never true, but I\nforced myself to accept it.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Nat_m01: <BLN>A prestigious house.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hri_m01_001: There's no shortage of Aragonian soldiers here.\nThe younger ones greet me eagerly as I pass by.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hri_m01_002: If Creek the Green can give them a little hope,\na little inspiration, then that's not a bad thing.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hri_m01_003: Though...I might want to keep an eye on them and\nensure they don't charge into battle rashly.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Hri_m01_004: I have experience dealing with hotheads.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Hri_m01: <BLN>They're so eager.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ann_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ann_m01_001: You wouldn't guess it, but I really was once a priest\nof Lord Solel himself.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ann_m01_002: After the Divine Emperor killed him, I was left\ndirectionless for a while.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Ann_m01_003: I couldn't possibly serve a Divine Emperor who'd\ndo such a thing.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Ann_m01: <BLN>I really was a priest.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mys_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mys_m01_001: 
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mys_m01_002: 
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mys_m01_003: 
MID_LGA_3_M03_Mys_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cle_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cle_m01_001: 
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cle_m01_002: 
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cle_m01_003: 
MID_LGA_3_M03_Cle_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M03_Jun_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Jun_m01_001: I feel sorry for Solel. His death at the hands of Dagda\nwas a tragedy.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Jun_m01_002: Solel always regretted not standing up to Dagda\nwhen his wife was executed.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Jun_m01_003: As do I... If it had been within my power, I would\nlike to have saved her.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Jun_m01: <BLN>I can't help but feel sorry for him.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mar_m01_001: He didn't make a show of it, but the Divine\nSovereign was really quite skilled with the spear.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mar_m01_002: Some even said my brother's abilities in combat\nexceeded mine.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mar_m01_003: And they weren't off the mark.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Mar_m01_004: If I'd clashed with him in his prime, I don't know\nwho would have won.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Mar_m01: <BLN>He was good with a spear.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Smi_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Smi_m01_001: My siblings have told me since I was a little\nSmyrnos that they can't tell what's on my mind.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Smi_m01_002: But it's easy to know if I'm thinking about something.\nIs it actually interesting? Then I am!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Smi_m01_003: Is it interesting enough to capture my attention?\nThen I'm always caught!
MID_LGA_3_M03_Smi_m01: <BLN>My siblings disappoint me.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cla_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cla_m01_001: I now understand that Fortuna lent you her power.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cla_m01_002: I'm surprised. Fortuna is our little sister. She's\nalways been unique among us.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cla_m01_003: She was always irritated, always unable to get\nalong with any of us brothers.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cla_m01_004: I never knew her to be the sort who takes any\naction whatsoever. So all this...surprises me.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Cla_m01_005: But now it finally makes sense how someone was\nable to destroy an underworld gate.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Cla_m01: <BLN>So, it was Fortuna?
MID_LGV_3_M03_Car_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Car_m01_001: It may sound like I'm making excuses, but we temple\ngods were not just sitting back and watching.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Car_m01_002: We were preoccupied trying to defend the perimeters\naround our temples.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Car_m01_003: To the point that it wasn't possible to coordinate or\nlaunch offensives.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Car_m01_004: When you reclaimed Dagsion, that all changed.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Car_m01_005: I'm truly grateful for your efforts, and pray for your\ncontinued success.
MID_LGA_3_M03_Car_m01: <BLN>I'm not just making excuses.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01_001: Oh, Promised One! I'm glad you seem to be in such\ngood spirits today!
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01_002: I'll tell you something that's been confusing me.\nYou seem familiar, but in the strangest way...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01_003: When I look at you as you are now, Father...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01_004: My heart feels so full that I'm almost overwhelmed.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01_005: Your mission to save the world was given to you by\nthe progenitor god, wasn't it?
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01_006: What a cruel thing to do to a dead man.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01_007: Well, you're alive now, so you're not actually a dead\nman, but still...
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01_008: From now on, I'll do everything I can to\nsupport you, Father.
MID_LGV_3_M03_Aur_m01_009: We are family, after all. And that is a precious thing!
MID_LGA_3_M03_Aur_m01: <BLN>Promised One!
MID_LGV_3_M03_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B01_m01_001: I found some pears growing in the forest and cooked\nthem up nice for everyone.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B01_m01_002: You know, I think things here are starting to settle\ndown a little bit.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B01_m01_003: It wasn't so long ago that eating food in public would\nmake you a target.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B01_m01: <BLN>Are things here settling down?
MID_LGV_3_M03_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B02_m01_001: Some of us who admire your bravery are forming\na citizen militia, Promised One.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B02_m01_002: I'm one of the founding members. We'll teach those\nrisen dead not to mess with Dagsion!
MID_LGA_3_M03_B02_m01: <BLN>We formed a citizen militia.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B03_m01_001: I just started training to fight. I'm still struggling to\nget the hang of handling a weapon.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B03_m01_002: But I can't give up. I need to learn to defend myself\nand not rely on anyone else to do it for me.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B03_m01: <BLN>I've started weapons training.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B04_m01_001: More and more people are taking up arms for that\nvolunteer force, or citizen militia, or whatever.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B04_m01_002: I hope they don't get too ambitious. Bravery alone\nwon't cut it against the risen dead.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B04_m01: <BLN>More people are taking up arms.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B05_m01_001: Um, Promised One? Even if it's just sometimes,\ncould you show up in my dreams?
MID_LGV_3_M03_B05_m01_002: Every night, I dream of my dead friend saying, "It\nhurts" and "I'm in pain" and stuff. Can you help?
MID_LGA_3_M03_B05_m01: <BLN>Hey, Promised One...
MID_LGV_3_M03_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B06_m01_001: We collect keepsakes from dead vulkans and temple\nsoldiers to try to get them to their next of kin.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B06_m01_002: But if their families lived in the capital, there's rarely\nanyone left to pass them on to.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B06_m01_003: If we can't identify a next of kin, there's not much\nwe can do with any personal effects. It's a shame...
MID_LGA_3_M03_B06_m01: <BLN>What's left goes to the next of kin.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B07_m01_001: We're still cleaning up the spaces around the temples,\nfor the sake of those who come to pray.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B07_m01_002: It's easier to get there if the roads are clear. Helps to\nput the mind at ease too.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B07_m01: <BLN>We're working on cleaning up.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B08_m01_001: This world is full of misery, but people still fall in\nlove and raise new life.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B08_m01_002: I'm pregnant myself—with the child of a man who\nwas killed fleeing the risen dead.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B08_m01_003: I came here today to pray for a happier future for\nthe little one.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B08_m01: <BLN>This world is full of misery, but...
MID_LGV_3_M03_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B09_m01_001: I'm positive that guy who showed up recently is the\nsame bandit who once laid waste to my field.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B09_m01_002: I don't like him being here, but where's he gonna go?\nThings are so bad all over that I can't hold a grudge.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B09_m01: <BLN>I'm certain that's him.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B10_m01_001: Another back tooth fell out. Probably because I'm\nundernourished.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B10_m01_002: It's not like I was living the high life before, but this...\nI don't think I'm going to make it.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B10_m01_003: Why'd I bother coming to Dagsion just to starve?\nI could've died at home.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B10_m01: <BLN>I'm not going to make it.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B11_m01_001: It's been some time since I took refuge here. I'm still\ngrateful they took in someone as destitute as me.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B11_m01_002: At least I have my health, right? There's got to be\na way for me to do my part, however small.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B11_m01: <BLN>I'm very grateful.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B12_m01_001: The misrule of King Gilchris made a mess of my\nhomeland of Arago.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B12_m01_002: But even he wasn't so callous as to kill every one of\nhis subjects. There's always someone worse, I guess.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B12_m01: <BLN>As bad as he was...
MID_LGV_3_M03_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B13_m01_001: I fled here with my son, but his wounds from the\nrisen dead were too severe, and he passed away.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B13_m01_002: At least I was able to bury him someplace nice\ninstead of a ditch on the side of the road.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B13_m01_003: You have to take what you can get these days.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B13_m01: <BLN>My son died.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B14_m01_001: My grandmother is dead. I thought she'd made it to\nsafety here, but no.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B14_m01_002: I'm sorry. You don't need to hear this while you're\ndoing your best to save us. Forget I brought it up.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B14_m01: <BLN>Why?
MID_LGV_3_M03_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B15_m01_001: I used to be a fisher, but I'm part of the citizen\nmilitia now.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B15_m01_002: I turned the tools of my trade into weapons. I won't\ngo fishing again until the world is at peace.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B15_m01: <BLN>I used to be a fisher.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B16_m01_001: This port was used by people from many nations,\nso all sorts of folks had dealings here.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B16_m01_002: Do you think when they hear how bad things are in\nDagda, they'll send someone to help us?
MID_LGV_3_M03_B16_m01_003: I mean, you showed up when you were needed.\nIs it really so strange that others might do the same?
MID_LGA_3_M03_B16_m01: <BLN>This port...
MID_LGV_3_M03_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B17_m01_001: My husband and I were Aragonian soldiers long ago.\nOne day, only his horse returned from battle.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B17_m01_002: I used to think he died honorably in combat, but get\nthis—he found himself a lover on the front lines!
MID_LGV_3_M03_B17_m01_003: I felt so stupid after praying every day that he'd come\nhome safe. Anyway, we're divorced now.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B17_m01: <BLN>Can you believe this?
MID_LGV_3_M03_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B18_m01_001: The Dagsion market was once a thriving place. Might\na few of the wares from those days be still around?
MID_LGV_3_M03_B18_m01_002: If I find something that looks like it'd sell, I pick it\nup, polish it, and sell it for a guaranteed profit!
MID_LGA_3_M03_B18_m01: <BLN>Any loose wares around here?
MID_LGV_3_M03_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B19_m01_001: Rather than remain a noble, I donated my private\nwealth to support the citizen militia.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B19_m01_002: I regret nothing. Survival is much more important\nthan prestige.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B19_m01: <BLN>I donated my private wealth.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M03_B20_m01_001: I see you've also come for the view, Promised One.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B20_m01_002: Do you know what people say about this place?
MID_LGV_3_M03_B20_m01_003: Vows sworn before Dagda's temple are supposed to\nhave a power that endures for eternity.
MID_LGV_3_M03_B20_m01_004: Maybe I should try bringing that girl that I like here.
MID_LGA_3_M03_B20_m01: <BLN>Do you know the legend?